<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick Moss</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1827">1827</a>–<a href="/years/1904">1904</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick Moss was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> politician who served as British Resident in the Cook Islands from 1891 to 1898. He persuaded the ariki of Rarotonga and the other islands to form a federal government with a parliament, the Cook Islands Federation, and promoted schools and laws. Criticised for his methods, he was recalled, and New Zealand annexed the islands in 1901.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-moss.jpg" alt="Frederick Moss" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Part of General Assembly Library : Parliamentary portraits · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frederick_Joseph_Moss.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
